        <mxCell id="p1-60" value="«use»" style="html=1;rounded=0;strokeColor=#333333;fontSize=10;labelBackgroundColor=#FFFFFF;dashed=1;endArrow=open;endSize=10;" parent="1" source="p1-28" target="p1-47" edge="1">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p1-61" value="" style="html=1;rounded=0;strokeColor=#333333;fontSize=10;labelBackgroundColor=#FFFFFF;endArrow=open;endSize=10;" parent="1" source="p1-38" target="p1-46" edge="1">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p1-62" value="1" style="edgeLabel;resizable=0;html=1;align=right;verticalAlign=bottom;fontSize=10;labelBackgroundColor=none;" parent="p1-61" connectable="0" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="0.78" relative="1" as="geometry">
            <mxPoint y="-6" as="offset" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p1-63" value="«return»" style="html=1;rounded=0;strokeColor=#333333;fontSize=10;labelBackgroundColor=#FFFFFF;dashed=1;endArrow=open;endSize=10;" parent="1" source="p1-38" target="p1-47" edge="1">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p1-64" value="&lt;b&gt;Design notes&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;• &lt;b&gt;Facade&lt;/b&gt; (GoF 1994, p. 185): PcBuildSession offers one coarse-grained interface over PcBuilder, CompatibilityChecker, SnapshotHistory and DefaultRules; clients only receive the read-only BuildView, never the mutable PcBuilder.&lt;br&gt;• &lt;b&gt;Caretaker protocol&lt;/b&gt; (GoF, p. 283): add()/remove() call history.save() &lt;i&gt;before&lt;/i&gt; mutating (snapshot-before-change); a new action clears the redo stack. undo()/redo() first push the &lt;i&gt;current&lt;/i&gt; state onto the opposite stack and then pop: a linear two-stack history. The caretaker never inspects a memento (narrow interface).&lt;br&gt;• &lt;b&gt;DefaultRules&lt;/b&gt; is a static factory (Bloch 2018, Item 1) that builds the rule catalogue (ids 1-40) as &lt;i&gt;data&lt;/i&gt;: behaviour is parameterised by Specification objects instead of subclassing." style="shape=note;size=12;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;backgroundOutline=1;fillColor=#FFFBE6;strokeColor=#D6B656;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;fontSize=10;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="700" width="620" height="162" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p1-65" value="&lt;b&gt;Observations&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;• &lt;b&gt;Command-query separation&lt;/b&gt; (Meyer 1997): canCheckout() is a query that prints WARNING violations as a side effect (stream peek), and prints the raw template message() with unresolved {PLACEHOLDERS}, not getMessage().&lt;br&gt;• Checkout is currently not referenced (its field in PcBuildSession is commented out); it only wraps PcBuilder.view().&lt;br&gt;• Types such as Supplier&amp;lt;Memento&amp;gt; appear in signatures only; the main.pattern package is intentionally not drawn.&lt;br&gt;• Visibility: + public, - private, ~ package-private; underlined = static." style="shape=note;size=12;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;backgroundOutline=1;fillColor=#FFFBE6;strokeColor=#D6B656;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;fontSize=10;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="700" y="700" width="640" height="133" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
