        <mxCell id="p6-85" value="&lt;b&gt;Data-structure notes&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;• &lt;b&gt;Inverted index&lt;/b&gt; (Manning et al. 2008, ch. 1): terms = ComponentType, postings = BuildRules whose specification dependsOn() that type. Instead of re-checking all |R| rules on every change, update(event) calls lookup({event.componentType()}), so only the rules in one postings list are re-evaluated; the full scan (evaluateAll) is reserved for RESTORED.&lt;br&gt;• &lt;b&gt;Complexity&lt;/b&gt;: add O(|keys|); remove O(|keys| &amp;middot; p) with p the postings length (ArrayList.remove(Object)); lookup O(&amp;Sigma;|postings|) and returns a LinkedHashSet, which de-duplicates rules reached through several keys while keeping a deterministic order. The index is an EnumMap pre-filled for every key (Bloch 2018, Item 37).&lt;br&gt;• The class is abstract although it declares no abstract method: abstractness only prohibits direct instantiation and fixes the intended extension point (RulesRegistry)." style="shape=note;size=12;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;backgroundOutline=1;fillColor=#FFFBE6;strokeColor=#D6B656;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;fontSize=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="1130" width="700" height="162" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p6-86" value="&lt;b&gt;Design notes&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;• &lt;b&gt;Registry&lt;/b&gt; (Fowler 2002, p. 480): name-to-rule map with fail-fast duplicate rejection, so the inverted index can never hold a &quot;ghost&quot; rule that is no longer reachable by name.&lt;br&gt;• &lt;b&gt;Observer&lt;/b&gt;: the constructor calls build.attach(this) and then evaluates all rules, giving a consistent initial state; registering &lt;i&gt;this&lt;/i&gt; from a constructor is a this-escape (safe here because the fields are initialised first and the code is single-threaded).&lt;br&gt;• ViolationList is an &lt;i&gt;idempotent upsert&lt;/i&gt; keyed by rule name (LinkedHashMap: O(1), insertion order): re-evaluating a rule replaces its previous violation, and a satisfied rule clears it.&lt;br&gt;• BuildRule validates every {PLACEHOLDER} in its message against ComponentType and against specification.dependsOn() at construction (fail-fast); Violation.getMessage() resolves them lazily, rendering &quot;none&quot; for empty lists." style="shape=note;size=12;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;backgroundOutline=1;fillColor=#FFFBE6;strokeColor=#D6B656;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;fontSize=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="780" y="1130" width="700" height="176" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
