        <mxCell id="p7-57" value="&lt;b&gt;Pattern notes&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;• &lt;b&gt;Specification&lt;/b&gt; (Evans &amp;amp; Fowler 1997; Evans 2003, ch. 9): a predicate object with isSatisfiedBy(candidate) that can be recombined with and / or / not. The combinators live in main.pattern.specification (not drawn): And, Or, Not, AndNot, OrNot and Implies extend CompositeSpecification, an instance of &lt;b&gt;Composite&lt;/b&gt; (GoF 1994, p. 163): primitive specifications are leaves, combinators are composites that delegate to their operands.&lt;br&gt;• &lt;b&gt;Implication&lt;/b&gt; is material implication A &amp;rArr; B &amp;equiv; &amp;not;A &amp;or; B (ImpliesSpecification). It is how &lt;i&gt;guarded rules&lt;/i&gt; are expressed, e.g. exactlyOne(CPU, MOTHERBOARD).implies(socketMatch). When the guard fails the rule holds &lt;i&gt;vacuously&lt;/i&gt;, which is why a guarded rule cannot itself be reused as a guard (see the note in RulesRegistry).&lt;br&gt;• Besides the Boolean answer, each specification exposes dependsOn(): a static footprint (set of ComponentType) that makes the specification usable as an index key in the inverted index of the rule package." style="shape=note;size=12;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;backgroundOutline=1;fillColor=#FFFBE6;strokeColor=#D6B656;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;fontSize=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="860" width="640" height="176" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p7-58" value="&lt;b&gt;Reconstruction notice&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;What is inferred and from where: BuildRule calls specification().isSatisfiedBy(PcBuilder) and specification.dependsOn(); DefaultRules chains Specs.* with .implies(...) / .or(...), so those methods return BuildSpecification; the field and factory names are taken verbatim from DefaultRules.java. Parameter names, field types and the way combinators propagate dependsOn() are assumptions. Send the two files to replace this page with an exact one." style="shape=note;size=12;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;backgroundOutline=1;fillColor=#FFFBE6;strokeColor=#D6B656;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;fontSize=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="720" y="860" width="620" height="118" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
